                                        "sense_id": "0e021e23-b37d-30ee-b3ad-3a99c3dcca5b",
                                        "entry_id": "bd14a103-0b64-32de-a16f-7ef82954d734",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A glossy, resinous material used as a surface coating; either a natural exudation of certain trees, or a solution of nitrocellulose in alcohol, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcc88458-f0e5-4f85-a018-989d6545ad93",
                                                "sense_id": "0e021e23-b37d-30ee-b3ad-3a99c3dcca5b",
                                                "text": "Had he deemed it \"wisest, best,\" Mr. O'Donagough was not without the means of furnishing a splendid mansion in very showy style, and yet not leaving a single morsel of lacker, or or-molu, unpaid for."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83107f7a-458c-445c-a1c3-04dfd8cecac8",
                                                "sense_id": "0e021e23-b37d-30ee-b3ad-3a99c3dcca5b",
                                                "text": "It is a solvent for nitrocellulose and vinyl chloride-acetate resins and may function as an antiblush agent in lacquers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1471898-4178-4e3a-9683-42a0dbce3cd4",
                                                "sense_id": "0e021e23-b37d-30ee-b3ad-3a99c3dcca5b",
                                                "text": "Cellosolves are used as solvents for lacquers, for sealing cellophane wrapping, and in hydraulic-brake fluid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2adfce32-bdf9-4ec5-bcd1-2a8cda20607f",
                                                "sense_id": "0e021e23-b37d-30ee-b3ad-3a99c3dcca5b",
                                                "text": "In place of traditional methods in which materials such as gesso, yellow ocher, powdered earth, liquid glue, and Japan tallow were used to obtain a gloss, and transparent lacquer was rubbed into the wood to protect it, materials such as artificially produced varoids and lacquer came into widespread use."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
